    "body": "## Summary\nServe LoRA adapters on GLM-5.3-Flash's KDA layers. Split out of #37753, rebased onto current sglang-miles; the rest of that PR (the glm53next port, KDA unfused layout under LoRA) is already on sglang-miles.\n\n## Changes\n- `lora/utils.py`: `b_proj`, `f_a_proj`, `f_b_proj`, `g_a_proj`, `g_b_proj` are known LoRA targets. `f_a_proj` / `g_a_proj` are replicated; `b_proj` / `f_b_proj` / `g_b_proj` shard their heads on the attention-TP group, like the KDA `qkv_proj` / `o_proj`.\n- `models/glm5_next.py`: `Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration.get_hidden_dim` sizes the buffers per layer. KDA and DSA layers differ in `o_proj`, and only KDA layers carry `qkv_proj` and the gates; other modules use `get_default_hidden_dim`.\n\n## Validation\nradixark/miles#3098 (native LoRA), GLM-5.3-Flash 4-layer slice, 8×H200, colocated, TP2/EP8 trainer, two TP4 engines, R3, lr 2e-3, 5 rollouts:\n- adapter served: `train/train_rollout_logprob_abs_diff` 0.0146 / 0.0175 / 0.0169 / 0.0168 / 0.0176\n- same run with the adapter not served (`--lora-train-only`): 0.0144 / 1.07 / 4.90 / 26.35 / 12.18\n- 76 adapter tensors per sync with `--check-lora-weight-equal`, no mismatch\n\nNot executed: the full 45-layer model; sglang-kernel 0.4.9 (validated on 0.4.7).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39011098381](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011098381)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39011098378](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011098378)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39011098397](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39011098397)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
